    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "{\"phase\": \"synthesis\", \"official_statement_as_data\": \"18th Marathon of Parallel Programming\\nSBAC-PAD & WSCAD – 2023\\nCalebe Bianchini1 and Roland Teodorowitsch2\\n1Mackenzie Presbyterian University\\n2Pontiﬁcal Catholic University of Rio Grande do Sul\\nRules for Remote Contest\\nFor all problems, read carefully the input and output session. For all problems, a sequen-\\ntial implementation is given, and it is against the output of those implementations that the\\noutput of your programs will be compared to decide if your implementation is correct.\\nYou can modify the program in any way you see ﬁt, except when the problem descrip-\\ntion states otherwise. You must upload a compressed ﬁle (zip) with your source code, the\\nMakeﬁle and an execution script. The script must have the name of the problem. You\\ncan submit as many solutions to a problem as you want. Only the last submission will\\nbe considered. The Makeﬁle must have the rule all, which will be used to compile your\\nsource code. The execution script runs your solution the way you design it – it will be\\ninspected not to corrupt the target machine.\\nThe execution time of your program will be measured running it with time program and\\ntaking the real CPU time given. Each program will be executed at least three times with\\nthe same input and the mean time will be taken into account. The sequential program\\ngiven will be measured the same way. You will earn points in each problem, correspond-\\ning to the division of the sequential time by the time of your program (speedup). The\\nteam with the most points at the end of the marathon will be declared the winner.\\nThis problem set contains 4 problems; pages are numbered from 1 to 7.\\n\\nGeneral Information\\nCompilation\\nYou should use CC or CXX inside your Makeﬁle. Be careful when redeﬁning them!\\nThere is a simple Makeﬁle inside you problem package that you can modify. Example:\\nFLAGS=-O3\\nEXEC=sum\\nCXX=icpc\\nall: $(EXEC)\\n$(EXEC):\\n$(CXX) $(FLAGS) $(EXEC).cpp -c -o $(EXEC).o\\n$(CXX) $(FLAGS) $(EXEC).o -o $(EXEC)\\nEach judge machine has its group of compilers. See them below and choose well when\\nwriting your Makeﬁle. The compiler that is tagged as default is predeﬁned in CC and\\nCXX variables.\\nmachine compiler command\\nhost GCC 13.2.0\\n(default)\\nC = gcc\\nC++ = g++\\nMPI\\nOpen MPI 4.1.2a1\\n(default)\\nC = mpicc\\nC++ = mpic++\\nGCC 13.2.0 C = gcc\\nC++ = g++\\ngpu\\nNVidia CUDA 12.0.1\\n(default)\\nC = nvcc\\nC++ = nvcc\\nGCC 8.3.1 C = gcc\\nC++ = g++\\nSubmitting\\nGeneral information\\nYou must have an execution script that has the same name of the problem. This script runs\\nyour solution the way you design it. There is a simple script inside you problem package\\nthat should be modiﬁed. Example:\\n#!/bin/bash\\n# This script runs a generic Problem A\\n# Using 32 threads and OpenMP\\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=32\\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=32 ./sum\\n\\nSubmitting MPI\\nIf you are planning to submit an MPI solution, you should compile usingmpiicc/mpiicpc.\\nThe script must call mpirun/mpiexec with the correct number of processes (max: 4). It\\nmust use a ﬁle called machines that are generated by the auto-judge system - do not\\ncreate it.\\n#!/bin/bash\\n# This script runs a generic Problem A\\n# Using MPI in the entire cluster (4 nodes)\\n# 'machines' file describes the nodes\\nmpirun -np 4 -machinefile machines ./sum\\nComparing times & results\\nIn your personal machine, measure the execution time of your solution using time pro-\\ngram. Add input/output redirection when collecting time. Use diff program to compare\\nthe original and your solution results. Example:\\n$ time -p ./A < original_input.txt > my_output.txt\\nreal 4.94\\nuser 0.08\\nsys 1.56\\n$ diff my_output.txt original_output.txt\\nDo not measure time and do not add input/output redirection when submitting your so-\\nlution - the auto-judge system is prepared to collect your time and compare the results.\\n\\nProblem A\\nNumber of Submatrices that Sum to k\\nLeonardo M. Takuno\\nGiven an M× N matrix A = (aij) of integers and k∈ Z, this problem1 involves counting\\nthe number of non-empty submatrices whose sums result in a given value k.\\nNote:\\n• The matrix may contain some negative numbers.\\n• Submatrix: A matrix obtained by removing some rows and/or columns from the\\nbeginning or/and from the end of a matrix.\\nFor example 1, given the following 2× 2 matrix and k = 1:\\n1 0\\n0 1\\nThe output is 6.\\nExplanation: Sum the element matrix[0][0], plus the element matrix[1][1], plus the two\\nsubmatrices line (1× 2), plus the two submatrices column (2× 1).\\nAs a second Example 2, given the following 2× 2 matrix and k = 0:\\n1 -1\\n-1 1\\nThe output is 5.\\nExplanation: Sum the two submatrices line ( 1× 2), plus the two submatrices column\\n(2× 1), plus 2× 2 submatrix.\\nYour assignment is to develop a parallel program for solving this problem.\\nInput\\nThe input contains only one test case. The ﬁrst line contains three integers: the value k\\n(−108≤ k≤ 108), the number of rows (M) and the number of columns (N) of a matrixA\\nseparated by a blank space (1≤ M, N < 1000). The next M lines contain N integers in\\neach line separated by blank space representingaij element of A (0≤ i < M, 0≤ j < N ,\\n−1000≤ aij≤ 1000).\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\nOutput\\nFor the test case print one line of output, and integer denoting the number of submatrices\\nthat sum to k.\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\n1based on LeetCode problem 1074.\\n1\\n\\nExample\\nSample input 1 Sample output 1\\n1 2 2 2\\n1 -1\\n-1 1\\n2\\n\\nProblem B\\nHighest Sum Path in Generic Tree\\nArthur F. Lorenzon\\nGiven a generic tree, your objective is to identify and calculate the path from the root to a\\nleaf that has the largest sum of node values. Each node in the tree has an associated value,\\nand a path is deﬁned as a sequence of nodes from the root to a leaf.\\nYour assignment is to develop a parallel program for solving this problem.\\nInput\\nThe ﬁrst input line has a unique integer N (1≤ N < 1500000), the number of nodes\\nin the tree. The next N lines describe the nodes. Each line begins with a decimal value\\nV (0.1≤ V ≤ 100.0), the node value, followed by an integer K (0≤ K≤ 1000), the\\nnumber of children. Then, there are K integers representing the children indices (starting\\nby 1).\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\nOutput\\nThe ﬁrst line must have the highest decimal value found. The second line must have the\\nindices that compose the path from the root to leaf with the highest sum. The indices must\\nbe split by Spaces and start by 1.\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\nExample\\nSample input 1 Sample output 1\\n5 Max Sum: 19.80\\n10.5 2 2 3 Path: 1 2 4\\n5.2 2 4 5\\n3.3 0\\n4.1 0\\n2.4 0\\n3\\n\\nProblem C\\nNPbonacci\\nRafael Castro, Wellington Martins\\nThe Fibonacci Sequence is a very well known recurrence, and we can describe any term\\nFi in the sequence, with i≥ 1, by the following:\\nFi =\\n\\n\\n\\n0, if (i = 1)\\n1, if (i = 2)\\nFi−1 + Fi−2, otherwise\\nIn the Fibonacci sequence the size of the base cases is two, the ﬁrst two values, F1 = 0\\nand F2 = 1 , are referred as base term, and any other term are constructed by using the\\nsum of the immediate two terms before.\\nAnother sequence called here asN P bonacciconsider a different set of base casesA, with\\nsize N. By consequence, any term that is not a base term, will consider the last N terms\\nin the sequence to construct its own value. But, instead of only a simple sum to construct\\nthe next term value, here is applied a weighted sum, multiplying the terms by a value\\ngiven by a list of integers P , where|P| = N. The N P bonacci can be described by the\\nfollowing:\\nF bi =\\n{\\nAi, if (i≤ N )∑N\\nk=1 F bi−k.Pk, otherwise\\nWe can notice, for example, that the N P bonacci sequence will be equal to the original\\nFibonacci, if we set N = 2, A = [0, 1] and P = [1, 1].\\nGiven the values N, H, the base cases A and the list P , compute the term F bH modulo\\n109 + 7.\\nYour assignment is to develop a parallel program for solving this problem.\\nInput\\nIn the ﬁrst line of the input you’ll receive two integers, N and H. In the second line, will\\nbe given N integers, A1A2A3...AN, representing the base cases A. In the third line and\\nlast line, will be given N integers, P1P2P3...PN, representing the list P .\\nConstraints:\\n• 1 ⩽ N ⩽ 1020;\\n• N < H ⩽ 109;\\n• 0 ⩽ Ai, Pi ⩽ 109, i = 1, . . . , N.\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\n4\\n\\nOutput\\nCompute the value of F bH modulo 109 + 7.\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\nExamples\\nSample input 1 Sample output 1\\n2 10 34\\n0 1\\n1 1\\nSample input 2 Sample output 2\\n3 50 783060858\\n2 2 2\\n1 2 1\\n5\\n\\nProblem D\\nNumber of ways to traverse a grid\\nSalles V . G. Magalhaes\\nGiven a matrix M (with dimensions NxN), the objective is to count the number of pos-\\nsible ways to traverse the matrix from cell (0,0) to cell (N− 1,N− 1), considering each\\nmove can only be done by either going to the right (increasing the x coordinate) or up\\n(increasing the y coordinate).\\nIn this version of the problem we have another restriction: some cells are blocked and,\\nthus, no path can traverse them.\\nThe proposed baseline algorithm employs dynamic programming to solve the problem.\\nYour assignment is to develop a parallel program for solving this problem.\\nInput\\nThe input has only one test case. The ﬁrst line contains two integers N and M (0 < N <\\n2× 105). N represents the dimension of the matrix and M is the number of blocked cells\\n(M < 0.01× N 2 when N is large (greater than 1000)). Then, there are M rows, each\\ncontaining the y and x coordinates of a blocked cell.\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\nOutput\\nThe output contains a single line. Print the number of paths from cell ( 0,0) to cell (N−\\n1,N− 1). You should print the answer modulus 1000000007 (since it may be big).\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\nExample\\nSample input 1 Sample output 1\\n3 1 3\\n1 0\\nSample input 2 Sample output 2\\n3 0 6\\n6\\n\\nSample input 3 Sample output 3\\n4 0 20\\n7\", \"current_sources_as_data\": {\"src/solution.cpp\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nconst int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n,m;\\n\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n\\t\\tint i,j;\\n\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n\\n\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n\\n\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n\\n\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\n\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n}\"}, \"automatic_observations_as_data\": {\"sources\": [{\"id\": \"f6306d74a90f4bd8\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"46175b227f8916033ab0d6ab938b51b4191dc3ff\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace row-wise recurrence with two rolling, zero-padded antidiagonal buffers.\", \"Group blockers by antidiagonal and zero their results before advancing.\", \"Use bounded unsigned NEON modular addition with a portable scalar fallback.\", \"Disable synchronized iostream input.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.00814021130402883, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..087ba48 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,77 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n+#include <cstdint>\\n #include <iostream>\\n+#include <utility>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n-using namespace std;\\n+#if defined(__aarch64__)\\n+#include <arm_neon.h>\\n+#endif\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+namespace {\\n+constexpr std::uint32_t MOD = 1000000007u;\\n \\n+void update_diagonal(const std::uint32_t* __restrict previous,\\n+                     std::uint32_t* __restrict current,\\n+                     int begin, int end) {\\n+    int row = begin;\\n+#if defined(__aarch64__)\\n+    const uint32x4_t modulus = vdupq_n_u32(MOD);\\n+    for (; row + 4 <= end; row += 4) {\\n+        const uint32x4_t left = vld1q_u32(previous + row);\\n+        const uint32x4_t above = vld1q_u32(previous + row - 1);\\n+        const uint32x4_t sum = vaddq_u32(left, above);\\n+        // Each sum is below 2*MOD. Unsigned underflow makes the\\n+        // subtracted value larger when no reduction is required.\\n+        const uint32x4_t reduced =\\n+            vminq_u32(sum, vsubq_u32(sum, modulus));\\n+        vst1q_u32(current + row, reduced);\\n+    }\\n+#endif\\n+    for (; row < end; ++row) {\\n+        const std::uint32_t sum = previous[row] + previous[row - 1];\\n+        current[row] = sum >= MOD ? sum - MOD : sum;\\n+    }\\n+}\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n+    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\\n+\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(std::cin >> n >> m)) {\\n+        return 0;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::vector<std::vector<int>> blocked_by_diagonal(2 * n - 1);\\n+    for (int obstacle = 0; obstacle < m; ++obstacle) {\\n+        int row, column;\\n+        std::cin >> row >> column;\\n+        blocked_by_diagonal[row + column].push_back(row);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Index -1 is a permanent zero sentinel. During the growing\\n+    // half, entries beyond the previous diagonal are still zero.\\n+    std::vector<std::uint32_t> first(n + 1, 0);\\n+    std::vector<std::uint32_t> second(n + 1, 0);\\n+    std::uint32_t* previous = first.data() + 1;\\n+    std::uint32_t* current = second.data() + 1;\\n+    previous[0] = blocked_by_diagonal[0].empty() ? 1u : 0u;\\n+\\n+    for (int diagonal = 1; diagonal < 2 * n - 1; ++diagonal) {\\n+        const int begin = std::max(0, diagonal - n + 1);\\n+        const int end = std::min(n, diagonal + 1);\\n+\\n+        // Both predecessors belong to the preceding diagonal,\\n+        // so every update in this interval is independent.\\n+        update_diagonal(previous, current, begin, end);\\n+        for (int row : blocked_by_diagonal[diagonal]) {\\n+            current[row] = 0;\\n+        }\\n+        std::swap(previous, current);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::cout << previous[n - 1] << '\\\\n';\\n+    return 0;\\n+}\"}, {\"id\": \"919357e09c7e47e5\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"a77e2a2ce1ff2cb450c6e22a1ae38c545956dc48\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Fuse two antidiagonals into one sweep without storing the intermediate wavefront.\", \"Reuse preceding input and intermediate lanes through NEON vector shifts.\", \"Sort intermediate blockers to form branch-free SIMD segments; apply second-wavefront blockers after the sweep.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.008355428154269854, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..c2c87c0 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,118 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n+#include <cstdint>\\n #include <iostream>\\n+#include <utility>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n-using namespace std;\\n+#if defined(__aarch64__)\\n+#include <arm_neon.h>\\n+#endif\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+namespace {\\n+constexpr std::uint32_t MOD = 1000000007u;\\n \\n+// Compute two wavefronts over an obstacle-free segment of the first.\\n+// Carry is the preceding value on that intermediate wavefront.\\n+std::uint32_t update_pair_segment(\\n+    const std::uint32_t* __restrict previous,\\n+    std::uint32_t* __restrict current,\\n+    int begin, int end, std::uint32_t carry) {\\n+    int row = begin;\\n+#if defined(__aarch64__)\\n+    if (row + 4 <= end) {\\n+        const uint32x4_t modulus = vdupq_n_u32(MOD);\\n+        uint32x4_t preceding_input = vdupq_n_u32(previous[row - 1]);\\n+        uint32x4_t preceding_middle = vdupq_n_u32(carry);\\n+        do {\\n+            const uint32x4_t input = vld1q_u32(previous + row);\\n+            const uint32x4_t input_before =\\n+                vextq_u32(preceding_input, input, 3);\\n+            const uint32x4_t middle_sum = vaddq_u32(input, input_before);\\n+            const uint32x4_t middle =\\n+                vminq_u32(middle_sum, vsubq_u32(middle_sum, modulus));\\n+\\n+            const uint32x4_t middle_before =\\n+                vextq_u32(preceding_middle, middle, 3);\\n+            const uint32x4_t sum = vaddq_u32(middle, middle_before);\\n+            const uint32x4_t reduced =\\n+                vminq_u32(sum, vsubq_u32(sum, modulus));\\n+            vst1q_u32(current + row, reduced);\\n+\\n+            preceding_input = input;\\n+            preceding_middle = middle;\\n+            row += 4;\\n+        } while (row + 4 <= end);\\n+        carry = vgetq_lane_u32(preceding_middle, 3);\\n+    }\\n+#endif\\n+    for (; row < end; ++row) {\\n+        const std::uint32_t middle_sum = previous[row] + previous[row - 1];\\n+        const std::uint32_t middle =\\n+            middle_sum >= MOD ? middle_sum - MOD : middle_sum;\\n+        const std::uint32_t sum = middle + carry;\\n+        current[row] = sum >= MOD ? sum - MOD : sum;\\n+        carry = middle;\\n+    }\\n+    return carry;\\n+}\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n+    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\\n+\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(std::cin >> n >> m)) {\\n+        return 0;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::vector<std::vector<int>> blocked_by_diagonal(2 * n - 1);\\n+    for (int obstacle = 0; obstacle < m; ++obstacle) {\\n+        int row, column;\\n+        std::cin >> row >> column;\\n+        blocked_by_diagonal[row + column].push_back(row);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Index -1 is a permanent zero sentinel. Entries beyond the\\n+    // growing wavefront remain zero until they first become valid.\\n+    std::vector<std::uint32_t> first(n + 1, 0);\\n+    std::vector<std::uint32_t> second(n + 1, 0);\\n+    std::uint32_t* previous = first.data() + 1;\\n+    std::uint32_t* current = second.data() + 1;\\n+    previous[0] = blocked_by_diagonal[0].empty() ? 1u : 0u;\\n+\\n+    for (int diagonal = 1; diagonal < 2 * n - 1; diagonal += 2) {\\n+        const int begin = std::max(0, diagonal - n + 1);\\n+        const int end = std::min(n, diagonal + 1);\\n+        auto& blockers = blocked_by_diagonal[diagonal];\\n+        std::sort(blockers.begin(), blockers.end());\\n+\\n+        // Intermediate blockers split the fused sweep into independent\\n+        // obstacle-free segments. Duplicate blockers are processed once.\\n+        int position = begin;\\n+        std::uint32_t carry = 0;\\n+        for (int row : blockers) {\\n+            if (row < position) {\\n+                continue;\\n+            }\\n+            carry = update_pair_segment(previous, current, position, row, carry);\\n+            current[row] = carry;\\n+            carry = 0;\\n+            position = row + 1;\\n+        }\\n+        carry = update_pair_segment(previous, current, position, end, carry);\\n+\\n+        // The growing second wavefront has one additional high row.\\n+        // In the shrinking half, the extra low output is never read.\\n+        if (end < n) {\\n+            current[end] = carry;\\n+        }\\n+        for (int row : blocked_by_diagonal[diagonal + 1]) {\\n+            current[row] = 0;\\n+        }\\n+        std::swap(previous, current);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::cout << previous[n - 1] << '\\\\n';\\n+    return 0;\\n+}\"}, {\"id\": \"238405d0ef2e4385\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"201430fd4d4c355d865963fc015bcc83ac9af0a7\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Store packed blockers sorted by four-row band and column; merge same-column events into row masks.\", \"Process clear spans in four-row, two-column microtiles using local left-neighbor state and one contiguous DP boundary array.\", \"Remove per-cell obstacle lookups, row copies and remainder operations; reduce sums with one conditional subtraction.\", \"Disable standard-stream synchronization and input tying.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.012593942073484262, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..91db8b5 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,103 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n+#include <cstddef>\\n #include <iostream>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n-using namespace std;\\n+namespace {\\n+const int MOD = 1000000007;\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+template <int Rows>\\n+inline void openSpan(int* dp, int begin, int end, int (&left)[Rows]) {\\n+    int x = begin;\\n+    for (; x + 1 < end; x += 2) {\\n+        int first = dp[x];\\n+        int second = dp[x + 1];\\n+        for (int row = 0; row < Rows; ++row) {\\n+            first += left[row];\\n+            if (first >= MOD) first -= MOD;\\n+            second += first;\\n+            if (second >= MOD) second -= MOD;\\n+            left[row] = second;\\n+        }\\n+        dp[x] = first;\\n+        dp[x + 1] = second;\\n+    }\\n+    if (x < end) {\\n+        int value = dp[x];\\n+        for (int row = 0; row < Rows; ++row) {\\n+            value += left[row];\\n+            if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\\n+            left[row] = value;\\n+        }\\n+        dp[x] = value;\\n+    }\\n+}\\n \\n+template <int Rows>\\n+void processBand(int* dp, int n, const std::vector<unsigned int>& events) {\\n+    int left[Rows] = {0};\\n+    int nextColumn = 0;\\n+    std::size_t event = 0;\\n+\\n+    while (event < events.size()) {\\n+        const int column = static_cast<int>(events[event] >> 2);\\n+        openSpan<Rows>(dp, nextColumn, column, left);\\n+\\n+        unsigned int mask = 0;\\n+        do {\\n+            mask |= 1u << (events[event] & 3u);\\n+            ++event;\\n+        } while (event < events.size() &&\\n+                 static_cast<int>(events[event] >> 2) == column);\\n+\\n+        int value = dp[column];\\n+        for (int row = 0; row < Rows; ++row) {\\n+            if (mask & (1u << row)) {\\n+                value = 0;\\n+            } else {\\n+                value += left[row];\\n+                if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\\n+            }\\n+            left[row] = value;\\n+        }\\n+        dp[column] = value;\\n+        nextColumn = column + 1;\\n+    }\\n+    openSpan<Rows>(dp, nextColumn, n, left);\\n+}\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n+    std::cin.tie(0);\\n+\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(std::cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\\n+\\n+    const int bandCount = (n + 3) / 4;\\n+    std::vector<std::vector<unsigned int> > blockers(bandCount);\\n+    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\\n+        int y, x;\\n+        std::cin >> y >> x;\\n+        blockers[y / 4].push_back(\\n+            (static_cast<unsigned int>(x) << 2) |\\n+            static_cast<unsigned int>(y & 3));\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::vector<int> dp(n, 0);\\n+    dp[0] = 1;\\n+    for (int band = 0; band < bandCount; ++band) {\\n+        std::vector<unsigned int>& events = blockers[band];\\n+        std::sort(events.begin(), events.end());\\n+        const int rows = std::min(4, n - 4 * band);\\n+        switch (rows) {\\n+            case 4: processBand<4>(&dp[0], n, events); break;\\n+            case 3: processBand<3>(&dp[0], n, events); break;\\n+            case 2: processBand<2>(&dp[0], n, events); break;\\n+            case 1: processBand<1>(&dp[0], n, events); break;\\n+        }\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    std::cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\\\n';\\n+    return 0;\\n+}\"}, {\"id\": \"6082a4a65d95450b\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"958a3c3b15e73c9ee9e845251d513128cab221ad\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Use static OpenMP work sharing across independent tiles on each diagonal, with at most four threads.\", \"Retain only north and west frontiers, eliminating row copies and requiring one barrier per tile diagonal.\", \"Align frontiers to avoid inter-tile false sharing and retain serial execution below a thread-granularity threshold.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.013086213730275631, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..9687076 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,90 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n+#include <cstdint>\\n #include <iostream>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n+#ifdef _OPENMP\\n+#include <omp.h>\\n+#endif\\n+\\n using namespace std;\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+static const int MOD = 1000000007;\\n+static const int TILE = 64;\\n+\\n+static int* aligned_data(vector<int>& storage) {\\n+    uintptr_t address = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(storage.data());\\n+    address = (address + 63) & ~uintptr_t(63);\\n+    return reinterpret_cast<int*>(address);\\n+}\\n \\n+static inline void scan_rectangle(\\n+    int y_begin, int y_end, int x_begin, int x_end,\\n+    const vector<vector<bool> >& blocked, int* dp, int* right) {\\n+    for (int y = y_begin; y < y_end; ++y) {\\n+        int left = right[y];\\n+        const vector<bool>& row = blocked[y];\\n+        for (int x = x_begin; x < x_end; ++x) {\\n+            int value = dp[x] + left;\\n+            if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\\n+            left = row[x] ? 0 : value;\\n+            dp[x] = left;\\n+        }\\n+        right[y] = left;\\n+    }\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n+    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n+\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\\n+\\n+    vector<vector<bool> > blocked(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\\n+    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\\n+        int y, x;\\n+        cin >> y >> x;\\n+        blocked[y][x] = true;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    // Align tile boundaries so concurrent tiles do not share frontier cache lines.\\n+    vector<int> dp_storage(n + 16, 0);\\n+    vector<int> right_storage(n + 16, 0);\\n+    int* dp = aligned_data(dp_storage);\\n+    int* right = aligned_data(right_storage);\\n+\\n+    // A single virtual incoming path seeds the origin.\\n+    dp[0] = 1;\\n+\\n+#ifdef _OPENMP\\n+    const int tile_count = (n + TILE - 1) / TILE;\\n+    const int workers = min(4, omp_get_max_threads());\\n+    if (workers > 1 && tile_count >= 2 * workers) {\\n+        #pragma omp parallel num_threads(workers)\\n+        {\\n+            for (int wave = 0; wave < 2 * tile_count - 1; ++wave) {\\n+                const int first = max(0, wave - tile_count + 1);\\n+                const int last = min(tile_count - 1, wave);\\n+\\n+                #pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n+                for (int tile_y = first; tile_y <= last; ++tile_y) {\\n+                    const int tile_x = wave - tile_y;\\n+                    const int y_begin = tile_y * TILE;\\n+                    const int x_begin = tile_x * TILE;\\n+                    scan_rectangle(y_begin, min(n, y_begin + TILE),\\n+                                   x_begin, min(n, x_begin + TILE),\\n+                                   blocked, dp, right);\\n+                }\\n+                // The implicit barrier publishes north and west tile boundaries.\\n+            }\\n+        }\\n+    } else\\n+#endif\\n+    {\\n+        scan_rectangle(0, n, 0, n, blocked, dp, right);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\\\n';\\n+    return 0;\\n+}\"}, {\"id\": \"7503402b0567423f\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"a57fc146b74e4b49fbf1349e7f3c558efe49e3f2\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Use at most four persistent threads, with at least 1024 columns per requested thread and a serial fallback for smaller grids.\", \"Compute zero-carry chunk scans, compose blocker-aware affine summaries, and correct only columns preceding each chunk's first blocker.\", \"Use one in-place DP row and bounded conditional modular subtraction instead of row copies and remainder operations.\", \"Disable synchronized iostream input without changing input or output formats.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.016305488534271717, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..860b20a 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,136 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n #include <iostream>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n+#ifdef _OPENMP\\n+#include <omp.h>\\n+#endif\\n+\\n using namespace std;\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+const int MOD = 1000000007;\\n+\\n+#ifdef _OPENMP\\n+struct alignas(64) ChunkSummary {\\n+    int tail;\\n+    int resets;\\n+};\\n+#endif\\n+\\n+static int countPaths(const vector<vector<bool> >& blockedCells) {\\n+    const int n = static_cast<int>(blockedCells.size());\\n+    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\\n+    dp[0] = 1;\\n+\\n+#ifdef _OPENMP\\n+    const int minColumnsPerThread = 1024;\\n+    int threads = min(4, omp_get_max_threads());\\n+    threads = min(threads, max(1, n / minColumnsPerThread));\\n+\\n+    if (threads > 1) {\\n+        ChunkSummary summaries[4] = {};\\n+\\n+        #pragma omp parallel num_threads(threads)\\n+        {\\n+            const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\\n+            const int teamSize = omp_get_num_threads();\\n+            const int begin = n * tid / teamSize;\\n+            const int end = n * (tid + 1) / teamSize;\\n+\\n+            for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\\n+                const vector<bool>& blocked = blockedCells[row];\\n+                int firstBlocked = end;\\n+                int left = 0;\\n+\\n+                // Scan this chunk with zero incoming horizontal carry.\\n+                for (int col = begin; col < end; ++col) {\\n+                    if (blocked[col]) {\\n+                        left = 0;\\n+                        if (firstBlocked == end) {\\n+                            firstBlocked = col;\\n+                        }\\n+                    } else {\\n+                        left += dp[col];\\n+                        if (left >= MOD) {\\n+                            left -= MOD;\\n+                        }\\n+                    }\\n+                    dp[col] = left;\\n+                }\\n+\\n+                summaries[tid].tail = left;\\n+                summaries[tid].resets = (firstBlocked != end);\\n \\n+                #pragma omp barrier\\n+\\n+                // A chunk maps an incoming carry x to either x + tail\\n+                // or tail, depending on whether it contains a blocker.\\n+                int incoming = 0;\\n+                for (int chunk = 0; chunk < tid; ++chunk) {\\n+                    if (summaries[chunk].resets) {\\n+                        incoming = summaries[chunk].tail;\\n+                    } else {\\n+                        incoming += summaries[chunk].tail;\\n+                        if (incoming >= MOD) {\\n+                            incoming -= MOD;\\n+                        }\\n+                    }\\n+                }\\n+\\n+                // Only the prefix before the first blocker depends on x.\\n+                if (incoming != 0) {\\n+                    for (int col = begin; col < firstBlocked; ++col) {\\n+                        int value = dp[col] + incoming;\\n+                        if (value >= MOD) {\\n+                            value -= MOD;\\n+                        }\\n+                        dp[col] = value;\\n+                    }\\n+                }\\n+\\n+                #pragma omp barrier\\n+            }\\n+        }\\n+\\n+        return dp[n - 1];\\n+    }\\n+#endif\\n+\\n+    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\\n+        const vector<bool>& blocked = blockedCells[row];\\n+        int left = 0;\\n+        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\\n+            if (blocked[col]) {\\n+                left = 0;\\n+            } else {\\n+                left += dp[col];\\n+                if (left >= MOD) {\\n+                    left -= MOD;\\n+                }\\n+            }\\n+            dp[col] = left;\\n+        }\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    return dp[n - 1];\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n+    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n+\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) {\\n+        return 0;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    vector<vector<bool> > blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\\n+    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\\n+        int row, col;\\n+        cin >> row >> col;\\n+        blockedCells[row][col] = true;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    cout << countPaths(blockedCells) << '\\\\n';\\n+    return 0;\\n+}\"}, {\"id\": \"345bddeac5f04c09\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"caa9b12b49310073f4016ad408d7bbfd2624ec39\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/solution.cpp\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace the two rolling DP rows and row copies with one array, retaining the updated left value in a scalar.\", \"Store blockers as sorted, deduplicated per-row column lists and process contiguous open spans without per-cell obstacle lookups.\", \"Replace per-cell remainder with one conditional subtraction; two reduced residues fit in signed 32-bit arithmetic.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.02343729759256045, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/solution.cpp b/src/solution.cpp\\nindex a92269b..9e1eb63 100644\\n--- a/src/solution.cpp\\n+++ b/src/solution.cpp\\n@@ -1,42 +1,54 @@\\n+#include <algorithm>\\n #include <iostream>\\n #include <vector>\\n \\n using namespace std;\\n \\n-const int MOD = 1000000007; //since the answer may grow a lot, we use the modulus\\n+const int MOD = 1000000007;\\n \\n+static inline void updateOpenSpan(int* dp, int begin, int end) {\\n+    int left = 0;\\n+    for (int col = begin; col < end; ++col) {\\n+        int value = dp[col] + left;\\n+        if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\\n+        dp[col] = value;\\n+        left = value;\\n+    }\\n+}\\n \\n int main() {\\n-\\tint n,m;\\n-\\tcin >> n >> m;\\n-\\tvector<vector<bool> >  blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n,false));\\n-\\tfor(int c =0;c<m;c++) {\\n-\\t\\tint i,j;\\n-\\t\\tcin >> i >> j;\\n-\\t\\tblockedCells[i][j] = true;\\t\\t\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\tvector<vector<int> > dp(2,vector<int>(n,0));\\n-\\n-\\tif(!blockedCells[0][0])\\n-\\t\\tdp[0][0] = 1;\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int j=1;j<n;j++) if(!blockedCells[0][j]) dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1];\\n-\\tdp[1][n-1] = dp[0][n-1];\\n-\\n-\\tfor(int i=1;i<n;i++) {\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) {\\n-\\t\\t\\tint ans = 0;\\n-\\t\\t\\tif(!blockedCells[i][j]) {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tans = dp[0][j];\\n-\\t\\t\\t\\tif(j!=0) ans += dp[1][j-1];\\n-\\t\\t\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\t\\tdp[1][j] = ans% MOD;\\n-\\t\\t}\\n-\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) dp[0][j] = dp[1][j];\\n-\\t}\\n-\\n-\\t\\n-\\tcout << dp[1][n-1] << endl;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+    int n, m;\\n+    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\\n+\\n+    vector<vector<int> > blockedColumns(n);\\n+    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\\n+        int row, col;\\n+        cin >> row >> col;\\n+        blockedColumns[row].push_back(col);\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\\n+        vector<int>& columns = blockedColumns[row];\\n+        sort(columns.begin(), columns.end());\